  "notes": [
    "The immutable AggregationRouter runtime, CREATE2-deployed with no proxy or configurable state, contains the unvalidated executor call. Users' approvals only set how much could be drained.",
    "Exact victim debits from receipt Transfer logs (plus Etherscan-indexed CW20-pointer transfers) of 4008 legs in 2601 successful drain transactions through both Kame routers, 2025-09-12 to block 234150523. Each debit is valued at its hourly DefiLlama price; only stablecoins, wrapped SEI/BTC/ETH/FRAX and liquid staking tokens are valued. Memecoins (about 116.8k USD at DefiLlama prices, excluded because the attackers' disposal likely moved thin markets) and 26 unpriced tokens are left out, so this is a conservative gross figure. Drains through the prior router 0x1415e8ee... (same defect, same campaign, 3978 USD) are merged. White-hat drains and the attacker's later return of 185 ETH are not deducted. Approvals were never revoked onchain by the protocol, and the campaign was still running at the data cutoff (block 234700000)."
  ]
